hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17679","Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad al-Ifriqi, from Ziyad ibn Nu'aym al-Hadrami, from Ziyad ibn al-Harith al-Suda'i, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Call the adhan, O brother of Suda'. He said: I called the adhan, and that was when dawn broke. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, he stood for prayer, and Bilal wanted to perform the iqamah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The brother of Suda' performs the iqamah, for whoever calls the adhan performs the iqamah."
"17680","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ya'la ibn Hakim, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Rafi' ibn Khadij, who said: We used to sharecrop at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a third and a fourth, or for specified food. He said: One of my uncles came to us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us a matter that was beneficial for us, and obedience to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is more exalted and more beneficial for us. He said: We said: What is that? He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or let his brother cultivate it, and let him not lease it for a third, nor a fourth, nor for specified food. Qatadah said: And he is Zahir."
